  "solution": {
    "text": "Acidic strength of dicarboxylic acid is based on the +I effect of alkyl group. As +I increases acidic nature decreases.<br />Compounds with formula <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> are called dicarboxylic acid.<br />Acidic strength order is:<br />Oxalic acid &gt; Malonic acid &gt; Succinic acid &gt; Glutaric acid",
